  ],
  "text": "Goosebumps are your body trying to fluff up hair you no longer have. On a furry animal it works. The coat puffs up and traps a layer of warm air. Every hair has a tiny muscle at its root whose only job is to yank it upright. Cold, or fear, and every one of those muscles fires at once. On a cat that doubles its size. On you it makes bumps. And it is not the only thing you kept long after you stopped using it. Wisdom teeth. A tailbone. Ear muscles almost nobody can still operate. Press your thumb and little finger together, then look at your wrist. Your body is still running instructions written for a body you stopped having. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
